      "body": "Concept ACK!\r\nSince #34897 the locator can lag the in-memory tip while `SetBestBlockIndex()` still advances the lock on every update, so should we maybe derive the lock from the committed locator instead (initialize in `Init()`, advance in `Commit()`, cap at the chain height on reorg, flush and drain before `pruneblockchain`) and cover it with a prune-mode index test?",
