      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "> Since https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34897 the locator can lag the in-memory tip while SetBestBlockIndex() still advances the lock on every update, so should we maybe derive the lock from the committed locator instead (initialize in Init(), advance in Commit(), cap at the chain height on reorg, flush and drain before pruneblockchain) and cover it with a prune-mode index test?\r\n\r\nThat seems out of scope for what this is fixing. If you have an unpruned node, and then add both a new index and a prune value to the config and restart, it will break on indexing because it will prune first before syncing the index. This is not about a lagging locator, but startup failing to lock the prune height for an empty index.",
      "user": {
        "login": "andrewtoth",
        "id": 237213,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIzNzIxMw==",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/237213?v=4",
